From ca211e68cc58bee8490dfde0b84a103f2804501d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stanislaw Grams <stanislaw.grams@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:55:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] OvmfPkg/IntelTdx: Enable Secure Boot and drop the shell by
 default

The Config-B TDX firmware shipped with SECURE_BOOT_ENABLE=FALSE and
BUILD_SHELL=TRUE by default, so a default production build performed no
Secure Boot image verification and embedded the full UEFI Shell, giving an
attacker an unauthenticated command environment.

Default SECURE_BOOT_ENABLE to TRUE and BUILD_SHELL to FALSE, matching the
hardened AmdSevX64 posture. Both remain overridable on the build command
line (-D FLAG=VALUE) for development. With Secure Boot enabled the shell FV
is already excluded by ShellDxe.fdf.inc.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Grams <stanislaw.grams@intel.com>
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/tianocore/edk2/commit/ca211e68cc58bee8490dfde0b84a103f2804501d]

---
 OvmfPkg/IntelTdx/IntelTdxX64.dsc | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/OvmfPkg/IntelTdx/IntelTdxX64.dsc b/OvmfPkg/IntelTdx/IntelTdxX64.dsc
index 69c42a9f5c..4f63a12640 100644
--- a/OvmfPkg/IntelTdx/IntelTdxX64.dsc
+++ b/OvmfPkg/IntelTdx/IntelTdxX64.dsc
@@ -29,13 +29,13 @@
   # Defines for default states.  These can be changed on the command line.
   # -D FLAG=VALUE
   #
-  DEFINE SECURE_BOOT_ENABLE      = FALSE
+  DEFINE SECURE_BOOT_ENABLE      = TRUE
   DEFINE DEBUG_TO_MEM            = FALSE
 
   #
   # Shell can be useful for debugging but should not be enabled for production
   #
-  DEFINE BUILD_SHELL             = TRUE
+  DEFINE BUILD_SHELL             = FALSE
 
   #
   # Device drivers
-- 
2.51.1

